<title>SPAIN: Lisbon air cargo rose five percent in January.</title>
<headline>Lisbon air cargo rose five percent in January.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo traffic at Lisbon airport rose 5.0 percent in January to 7,567 tonnes, the Portuguese airports authority ANA said.</p>
<p>Passenger numbers at Lisbon were 2.4 percent higher than the same month a year earlier at 415,368.</p>
<p>The number of aircraft movements rose by 1.5 percent in the month to 6,215.</p>
<p>Cargo business at Porto, usually the country's second biggest airfreight airport, was up 6.9 percent in January to 2,159 tonnes.</p>
<p>Last month, however, Ponta Delgada airport overtook Porto and handled 5,609 tonnes of cargo.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
